  "editorial_md": "### Intuition\nTwo strings are anagrams exactly when every letter occurs the same number of times in both. Order doesn't matter — only counts.\n\n### Algorithm\nIf the lengths differ, return `false`. Otherwise keep 26 counters: add one for each letter of `s`, subtract one for each letter of `t`. The strings are anagrams iff every counter ends at zero.\n\n```python\ndef isAnagram(s, t):\n    if len(s) != len(t):\n        return False\n    count = [0] * 26\n    for a, b in zip(s, t):\n        count[ord(a) - 97] += 1\n        count[ord(b) - 97] -= 1\n    return all(c == 0 for c in count)\n```\n\n### Complexity\nO(n) time and O(1) extra space (the alphabet is fixed). Sorting both strings and comparing is a simpler O(n log n) alternative.",
